    627  f24e							; LaserWallClamp $F25A (name+pin kept — sim_frame_budget beam_cols keys on
    628  f24e							; the entry; redesign 2026-10-08): CONTACT wall test — tests ONLY the
    629  f24e							; missile TIP cell (one display col x band rows RoomY+2..3) instead of
    630  f24e							; walking the whole swept path. The sweep/phase machine is gone: bank0
    631  f24e							; LaserInput now travels LaserX +/-4px/frame from the eye, capped at the
    632  f24e							; old sweep extent (RoomX+20 / max(RoomX-20,0)) and resets on contact, so
    633  f24e							; there is no path to clamp and CollisionX is never modified (old S6
    634  f24e							; mid-wall tip clamp retired with the sweep).
    635  f24e							; In (bank0 LaserInput .LaserGo): CollisionX = LaserX, drawn M0 = [A-7,A],
    636  f24e							; PlayerDir live, RoomY live, PF0Buf = the render map (bomb holes = air),
    637  f24e							; patch-strip marker = LineCount x OvHead/OvTail (LWpSetup, $F600).
    638  f24e							; M1 patch strip: tip px in [M1X-7, M1X] (M1X = (RoomPF0Lo)+14) = solid
    639  f24e							; A=2 — the mirror walk alone passes the cell (patch = open, envelope) and
    640  f24e							; the beam used to sail through the async block; kill-aware (b4 skip).
    641  f24e							;   right: tip px = A	      left: tip px = A-7 (A < 7 -> off-screen ->
