   1369  fc4c							; Room-exit handlers — MOVED from bank0 (C3, 2026-10-20; were $F4DB-$F535 = 90 B).
   1370  fc4c							; C1 (2026-10-20): LEVEL_FORMAT 2 — there is NO connection table any more. Each
   1371  fc4c							; room owns ONE grid-position byte (x<<4|y, normalised to the level origin) at
   1372  fc4c							; level base + n (C2 2026-10-20: the 3 B record is three columns, so the
   1373  fc4c							; position column still starts one block-of-n in), and an exit is resolved by
   1374  fc4c							; stepping that byte by a direction delta ($FF up / $01 down / $F0 left /
   1375  fc4c							; $10 right) and SCANNING the level's position column for a match (<= 20
   1376  fc4c							; iterations, cold path = room load only).
   1377  fc4c							;
   1378  fc4c							; Why no boundary guard is needed: a nibble of 15 never occurs in a stored
   1379  fc4c							; position (POSITION_SPAN = 15 in convert_level.py, nibble 15 = sentinel), and
   1380  fc4c							; stepping off the grid always wraps the moved nibble to 15 — so an exit past
   1381  fc4c							; the grid edge can never match a room. The old nibble-room-index pack capped a
   1382  fc4c							; level at 15 rooms; this lifts it to 225 grid cells (20 rooms/level with room
   1383  fc4c							; to spare) at 1 B/room instead of 2.
